      "message": "[error] Line 2918: 🔴 The strict raw `created` comparison rejects valid same-generation snapshots relayed by an older daemon. Legacy `ConvInfo` messages contain only second-resolution `created`, which `msgpack_unpack` reconstructs as `...000ms`; a newer daemon may have the same generation persisted with `createdMs` at `...123ms`. The legacy removal/erasure then hits this `continue` before `newerErasure` is evaluated, so the originating erasure is never applied and the repository remains. Preserve timestamp precision/provenance (or use an explicit generation identity) and compare legacy snapshots in a way that still distinguishes genuinely older generations; add a serialized old-peer regression test.",
